Dear Mr. Muradyl,

I attended the International Clean Air Dialogue in Istanbul on 23–24 September 2026, where I learned about MoveGreen's work in independent air-quality monitoring, public environmental data and advocacy.

I am developing GreenHope, an environmental intelligence platform that combines satellite Earth-observation data, Sentinel-2 imagery, NASA FIRMS active-fire data, thermal anomaly detection, field sensors and public air-quality information.

We are preparing a concept for the partner-development phase of XPRIZE Mission Methane, focusing on diffuse methane emissions from landfills, waste-management systems and wastewater facilities.

We are looking for a technical and civil-society partner who could help us:

1. Validate satellite and thermal-alert data with ground air-quality sensors;
2. Monitor waste-burning, landfill and environmental-risk hotspots;
3. Develop a baseline for methane, PM2.5 and other air-quality impacts;
4. Connect with a waste-management company or landfill operator;
5. Support responsible media engagement and public communication.

Could you advise whether MoveGreen would be interested in a technical or pilot collaboration, or introduce us to an appropriate waste-management, university or methane-measurement partner in Central Asia?

May I send you a short, non-confidential one-page concept note and arrange a brief introductory call?
